        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c50" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;" value="new (just)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="120" x="500" y="918" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c51" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;" value="✓ tomato early blight" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="280" x="620" y="918" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c52" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;" value="seen · cucumber anthracnose" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="250" x="40" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c53" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" value="−3.4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="110" x="290" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c54" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" value="97%" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="100" x="400" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c55" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;" value="new ✗" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="120" x="500" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c56" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;" value="✗ cucumber downy mildew" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="280" x="620" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c57" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#555555;fontSize=12;" value="Last row: a known disease wrongly sent to the new-pair specialist can only answer a new pair, so it is wrong whatever the specialist does. Typical mix: a known disease mistaken for the new disease of the &lt;b&gt;same crop&lt;/b&gt;." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="860" x="40" y="985" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c58" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#fff0f0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;Why &#39;no γ&#39; still means calibrated&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Every other model uses γ: a fixed handicap subtracted from all known pairs, so new pairs get a fair chance.&lt;br&gt;• Subtracting γ and then taking the top pair is the same as asking &#39;is the margin bigger than −γ?&#39;.&lt;br&gt;• The gate asks the same question about the same margin, with a cut-off learned on validation instead of a γ grid.&lt;br&gt;• So the gate &lt;b&gt;is&lt;/b&gt; calibration, done by a small classifier. Proof: on test it sends 20.6% of seen and 94.9% of unseen photos to the new pairs; v6.3 with γ = 6.7 sends 21.0% and 94.8%. HM 74.98 vs 74.99.&lt;br&gt;• Compare v15 with other models&#39; &lt;b&gt;calibrated&lt;/b&gt; HM, not their γ = 0 HM (v6.3 at γ = 0: 27.0)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="800" x="980" y="640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c59" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Colours&lt;/b&gt;: blue = CLIP model · orange = CNN model · yellow = gate · green = known-pair (seen) specialist · red = new-pair (unseen) specialist.&lt;br&gt;Test label space: 323 seen + 10 unseen = 333 pairs. On validation the &#39;new&#39; pairs are 20 seen pairs held out of training (pseudo-unseen)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="800" x="940" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p1" name="2 How it was fitted">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeight="1300" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="c2" value="v15: what was fitted, on which data, in which order" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;align=left;fontSize=20;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1500" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="One validation split (seed 42): 862 val-seen images + 533 pseudo-unseen images from 20 held-out seen pairs. Member scores reused from v6.3&#39;s cache (no retraining)." style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#555555;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="56" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;0. Member validation scores&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;v10.3 and ConvNeXt-Base retrained on the split by train/ensemble.py for v6.3; cached val_scores_*.npy reused (validation.reuse_val_scores_from)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="100" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="&lt;b&gt;1. Baselines (with γ)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each member alone and the one-weight mix, weight 0…1 step 0.1, γ grid 0–15. Best mix: weight 0.3 on v10.3 → val HM 66.02% (= v6.3)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="210" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c7" value="&lt;b&gt;2. Experts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Seen expert weight = best val-seen accuracy among seen pairs → 0.3 (90.60%; v10.3 85.15, ConvNeXt 90.26).&lt;br&gt;Unseen expert weight = best pseudo-unseen accuracy among unseen pairs → 0.3 (64.35%; v10.3 58.16, ConvNeXt 56.66)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="320" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c8" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c7">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c9" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Gate, out-of-fold&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Logistic regression on the 3 margins; label = is the image pseudo-unseen. GroupKFold(5) by pair, so each image&#39;s gate logit comes from a gate that never saw its pair. AUROC 0.921." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="430" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c10" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c7" target="c9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c11" value="&lt;b&gt;4. Routing choice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bias grid −6…+6 step 0.1 × {hard, soft}, scored by val HM on the out-of-fold logits → hard, bias 0.3, val HM 65.61% (seen 76.22, unseen 57.60)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="540" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c12" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c9" target="c11">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c13" value="&lt;b&gt;5. Refit gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gate refit on all validation images; experts, bias and mode frozen." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="650" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c14" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c11" target="c13">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c15" value="&lt;b&gt;6. Test once&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gate + experts applied to test-seen and test-unseen. HM 74.98%. Not used for any decision." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="760" width="1000" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c16" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c13" target="c15">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c17" value="&lt;b&gt;Feature sets tried for the gate (val HM, out-of-fold)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &#39;members&#39; (A and B: best seen, best unseen, confidences, agreement): 63.91%&lt;br&gt;• &#39;members+mix&#39; (same plus M): 64.42%&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&#39;margins&#39; (3 margins): 65.61% ← used&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fewer features generalise better to pairs the gate was not trained on." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100" y="100" width="600" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c18" value="&lt;b&gt;Follow-up detectors (2026-11-16, prototype, split 42 only)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Nearest-neighbour support in v10.3 / frozen CLIP / BioCLIP embeddings: AUROC up to 0.84 alone; with margins 63.5–66.1%.&lt;br&gt;• Training counts, shared crop / shared disease: 63.4–65.4%.&lt;br&gt;• Margins of four members (v10.3, v5.13, ConvNeXt-Base, ConvNeXt-Base 336): AUROC 0.926–0.927, never more than 0.6 above the same members&#39; γ ensemble.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AUROC stayed at 0.92–0.93 whatever the features." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100" y="370" width="600" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c19" value="&lt;b&gt;Why the gate is stuck&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;89% of misrouted val-seen images were confused with a pseudo-unseen pair &lt;b&gt;of their own crop&lt;/b&gt;. Val-seen images whose crop has no pseudo-unseen pair were misrouted only 3% of the time. Seen vs unseen is really a within-crop disease decision, so the gate is limited by disease recognition." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#fff0f0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100" y="700" width="600" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
